WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.202
-Republicans are making clear

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.904
that they have no interest
in hearing the truth

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.106
about Supreme Court nominee
Brett Kavanaugh.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.308
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:14.080
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.449
As the President faced
a growing crisis

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.184
over the sexual-assault
allegations

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.852
against his
Supreme Court nominee,

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.454
he flew to North Carolina

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.090
to survey damage
from Hurricane Florence.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.860
And as usual,
he was super weird about it.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.395
At one point,
according to reporters...

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.746
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:51.517
Oh, my God, I swear Trump could
see a guy jump off a building

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.686
and think,
"Oh, cool -- free shoes."

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.422
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.190
And in case you think
Trump was just kidding,

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.226
he later told reporters...

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.933
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.870
Ah, yes.
Who could forget

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.475
the famous Supreme Court case
of Finders v. Keepers.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.710
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.011
This is the guy...

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:21.280
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.683
That right there is the guy
who gets to pick

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:26.586
our next Supreme Court Justice,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.355
a man who thinks that,
legally speaking,

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:33.560
if a boat shows up on your lawn,
you get to keep it.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.027
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.329
And yet it's very much the case
that Republicans are hoping

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.331
Trump will be able
to reshape the Supreme Court

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:42.268
for a generation by rushing to
get his nominee Brett Kavanaugh

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.070
confirmed despite the credible

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.038
sexual-assault allegations
against him.

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:48.107
Republicans have been engaged
in a 40-year project

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.776
to install a conservative
majority on the court,

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:52.845
and Kavanaugh's nomination
was supposed to be

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.414
the crowning achievement
in that project.

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:57.316
And Trump was very proud
of his choice,

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:59.018
although he mainly
seemed concerned

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.387
with whether Kavanaugh
looked the part.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:05.524
-Hopefully, everything goes
very well with Judge Kavanaugh.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.260
He's central casting.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.461
You know, 10 years ago,

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.396
they said, "He'll be
a Supreme Court judge."

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.866
Justice Kavanaugh
is doing great.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:16.336
Looks like --
I don't know, very tough.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.603
Central casting.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:18.738
-I don't know.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.540
If he really
came from central casting,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.341
they wouldn't make him
a Supreme Court Justice.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:24.711
They'd make him
the manager on "Superstore."

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.612
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:29.148
And if you think Kavanaugh
would never lie,

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:32.118
here he is in his first remarks
as a Supreme Court nominee

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.787
in order to shamelessly
suck up to Trump.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:38.290
-Mr. President, thank you.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:43.062
Throughout this process,
I've witnessed firsthand

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:48.668
your appreciation for the vital
role of the American judiciary.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:53.239
No president
has ever consulted more widely

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:57.310
or talked with more people
for from more backgrounds

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:01.281
to seek input about
a Supreme Court nomination.

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:04.117
-There is absolutely no way
that is true.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.652
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.019
He might as well have said,

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:10.189
"No president has ever
looked better in a white Polo."

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:13.525
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:17.029
But Kavanaugh --
Kavanaugh was willing to lie

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.765
to please his boss because he's
been a loyal partisan Republican

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:21.133
for most of his career,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.769
someone conservatives know
they'll be able to depend on

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.237
to implement their agenda.

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:28.574
Trump himself even claimed he'd
heard Kavanaugh's name mentioned

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:31.543
as a possible Supreme Court
Justice for years.

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:33.412
-He's an outstanding intellect.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:36.115
He's an outstanding judge.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.750
He was born for the position.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.419
I heard as long as 10 years ago
people were saying

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:41.854
he should be
a Supreme Court judge.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.156
I didn't know him at the time,

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.157
but I was hearing
from a lot of people,

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:48.594
friends of mine from Washington
and other places,

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:49.996
saying that Brett Kavanaugh

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.964
should be
a Supreme Court judge someday.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.366
-No.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.733
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:57.403
You did not hear people saying
Brett Kavanaugh

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:00.706
should be a Supreme Court
Justice 10 years ago.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.475
10 years ago,
you were yelling at Gary Busey

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:05.611
for stealing
Meat Loaf's art supplies.

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.847
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:11.150
Kavanaugh's nomination
was the culmination

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.520
of a decades-long ideological
project to reshape the Court,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.188
and Republicans
are making it clear

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:17.824
that they want to see
that project through,

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:20.459
even if it means
ignoring a credible allegation

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:21.661
of sexual assault.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.028
Trump was asked
about the allegations

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:26.499
against Kavanaugh made
by Dr. Christine Blasey Ford.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.801
Trump said he wanted
the process to play out

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.937
while making clear
he was firmly behind Kavanaugh.

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:35.475
-We are looking to get this done
as quickly as possible.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.776
He is a truly
outstanding person, as you know.

00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:39.111
He is an incredible man.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.147
He's an incredible intellect.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.916
He will make an incredible
Supreme Court Justice,

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:47.353
but we feel that we want
to go through a process.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.788
We want to hear both sides.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.890
He can handle himself
better than anybody.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.825
He's a very outstanding man.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.828 line:0%
Thank you.
Thank you.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.997
-Oh, I'm totally supportive.
Yes, I'm very supportive.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:00.332
-You can't say you want
a fair and open process

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.635
but also that
you're supportive of one side.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.203
He's like a ref
at the Super Bowl saying,

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.571
"Let's have a good, clean game

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.740
so we can get that handsome
Tom Brady another trophy."

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.108
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:10.977
The White House is trying
to have it both ways.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.279
They're trying to insulate Trump
from the political fallout

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.813
if Kavanaugh's nomination
blows up

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:16.715
while also standing firmly

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:18.284
behind their
Supreme Court nominee.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.953
In fact, on Monday,
Kavanaugh was at the White House

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.421
for nine hours of meetings,

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:25.924
but White House staff made sure
to keep Trump away from him.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:28.094
-Inside the White House,
they were hunkered down,

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:30.028
closely monitoring everything,

00:05:30.028 --> 00:05:32.798
but keeping the judge away from
meeting with President Trump,

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:34.867
who was nearby
in the Oval Office,

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.803
meeting with officials, as well.
-Why?

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:39.172
-They don't meet, Chris,
based on my reporting,

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:41.073
because they want
to protect the President.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:43.108
-So, Kavanaugh
was in the building all day,

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:44.710
and they had to keep Trump
away from him.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.712
That means that, for nine hours,

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.814
it was someone's job
inside the White House

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:50.950
to keep Trump distracted.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.585
"Okay, guys,
gonna be a long day.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:55.254
Get me three remote controls,
an issue of "Juggs" magazine,

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.722
and a cheeseburger on a string.

00:05:56.722 --> 00:05:58.890
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.726
"Damn you, cheeseburger."

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:02.428
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.530
"The cheeseburger
won't stand still."

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.199
[ Applause ]

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:09.502
The Republicans' gambit here
is to make it seem like

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.136
they want a fair
and open process,

00:06:11.136 --> 00:06:14.173
but in reality, they want it
to look like a he said, she said

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.975
so they can just ignore it
and move on.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.443
They won't even
interview witnesses

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.077
or let the FBI investigate.

00:06:19.077 --> 00:06:20.479
They made it clear
that they either

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:22.748
don't believe Ford's story
or don't care.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.650
In fact, GOP Senators
are already insisting

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.585
that Ford must have
gotten her story wrong

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:29.321
or that she might be doing this
for political purposes.

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:32.391
-If Ms. Ford really did not
want to come forward,

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:36.262
never intended to come forward,
never planned to come forward,

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:38.764
why did she pay
for a polygraph in August,

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:40.766
and why did she
hire a lawyer in August

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:43.302
if she never intended
to do what she's doing?

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:45.971
-Senator Cornyn
this morning saying that

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:48.574
there are gaps in her story,
appear to be gaps in her story.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.742
-Do you think that this,
in any way,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:53.145
is going
to derail his nomination?

00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:55.581
-No. He's a straight-shooting,
honest guy.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:58.484
I think when people
listen to him, they'll know --

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.186
they'll know
that he's all right.

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:04.990
-And do you think that any of
these claims are legitimate?

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.226
-No, I don't.
I think --

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:10.629
I think this woman,
whoever she is, is mixed up.

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:12.598
-I love these old-ass Senators

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.734
claiming other people
are mixed up.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:15.968
Just to give you
some perspective,

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.770
here's that same Senator,
Orrin Hatch,

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.272
asking Mark Zuckerberg
a question about Facebook

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:22.007
at a hearing earlier this year.

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:23.609
-How do you sustain
a business model

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:26.879
in which users
don't pay for your service?

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:27.979
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.979 --> 00:07:31.116
-Senator, we run ads.

00:07:31.116 --> 00:07:32.285
-I see.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:34.286
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:36.255
-"Okay, okay.

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:40.326
But how do you get all the faces
inside the book?"

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:43.262
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:46.232
"And where do you
print this book?

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:47.767
Can I get the book
at Barnes &amp; Noble?

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.268
How many pages is the book?"

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:50.269
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.737
"How much does the book cost?

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.439
Is the book available on Kindle?

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:56.809
And a follow-up question --
what's a Kindle?"

00:07:56.809 --> 00:08:00.346
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:03.149
Republicans are making it
as clear as possible

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:04.583
they don't actually
have an interest

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:05.884
in hearing the truth
of what happened.

00:08:05.884 --> 00:08:08.220
They're rushing to get a man
accused of sexual assault

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.189
on the Supreme Court
because it's the culmination

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:12.358
of a 40-year project to solidify

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.660
their conservative majority
for a generation.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:15.861
If you're looking for villains,

00:08:15.861 --> 00:08:17.596
these guys
are straight out of...

00:08:17.596 --> 00:08:18.764
-Central casting.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:21.100
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.203
[ Cheers and applause ]

